# Git: main branch only

This project uses a single-branch workflow.

- **Always work on `main`** — never create feature branches, fix branches, or any other branch names.
- **Always push to `origin/main`** — remote: `https://github.com/novaxumair/cheats-intel.com.git`
- Do not run `git checkout -b`, `git switch -c`, or `git push origin <other-branch>`.
- After changes: `git add`, `git commit`, then `git push origin main` (or `git push` when on main with upstream set).
- If accidentally on another branch, switch back to `main` and merge or discard — do not leave stray branches on GitHub.
